Subject: [PATCH] rpi: keep discovered_ram_size out of .bss

Commit d19d9e1c064b ("rpi: Add a local get_effective_memsize()", in
v2026.10) added a static variable that dram_init() assigns before
relocation. Before relocation .bss overlays .rela.dyn, so the assignment
overwrites the r_info field of the second relocation entry with the RAM
size. relocate_code then skips that entry and one pointer in the relocated
U-Boot keeps its pre-relocation value.

In the Raspberry Pi 5 build the entry belongs to the list head
efi_runtime_mmio. efi_add_runtime_mmio() then stores a heap pointer through
the stale pointer, 0xfe8 bytes into the old U-Boot image at 0x80000, which
is kernel_addr_r: a file loaded there before the first EFI call is
corrupted. iPXE loaded that way hit an undefined instruction as soon as it
configured the network. Which pointer is hit depends on the build, so the
other models are affected in other ways.

Put the variable in .data, like fw_dtb_pointer next to it.
---
diff --git a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
index 1da5df9235..38af9487f2 100644
--- a/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
+++ b/board/raspberrypi/rpi/rpi.c
@@ -39,7 +39,12 @@ DECLARE_GLOBAL_DATA_PTR;
  */
 unsigned long __section(".data") fw_dtb_pointer;
 
-static phys_addr_t discovered_ram_size;
+/*
+ * Assigned in dram_init(), which runs before relocation. Until U-Boot has
+ * relocated, .bss overlays the relocation table (.rela.dyn), so keep this
+ * out of .bss: a write there turns a relocation entry into garbage.
+ */
+static phys_addr_t __section(".data") discovered_ram_size;
 
 /* TODO(sjg@chromium.org): Move these to the msg.c file */
 struct msg_get_arm_mem {
